---
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";
---

<DocsLayout title="SCIM Provisioning">
  <h1>SCIM 2.0 Provisioning</h1>
  <p>
    Identity exposes an inbound <strong>SCIM 2.0</strong> server (RFC 7643 /
    RFC 7644) under <code>/scim/v2</code> so an external identity provider —
    Okta, Microsoft Entra ID, Google Workspace — can lifecycle-manage users
    in a project: create accounts on hire, deactivate on offboard, and keep
    profile attributes in sync, all without anyone logging into an admin
    console.
  </p>

  <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/30 p-4 text-sm">
    <strong>Disabled by default.</strong> When
    <code>GATEWAY_SCIM_ENABLED</code> is unset the <code>/scim/v2/*</code>
    routes are never registered and return <code>404</code>. The headless
    RPCs are unaffected. Turning SCIM on requires a bearer token <em>and</em> a
    project id; the server refuses to boot otherwise.
  </div>

  <h2>Enable it</h2>
  <Code
    lang="bash"
    code={`# Turn on the SCIM server, set the shared bearer token the IdP presents,
# and bind it to the single project whose users it may provision.
GATEWAY_SCIM_ENABLED=true
GATEWAY_SCIM_BEARER_TOKEN=<a-long-random-secret>
GATEWAY_SCIM_PROJECT_ID=<project-id>`}
  />
  <p>
    Configure your IdP's SCIM connector with the base URL
    <code>https://&lt;your-host&gt;/scim/v2</code> and the same bearer token.
    The bearer token is bound to the single project named by
    <code>GATEWAY_SCIM_PROJECT_ID</code>: every SCIM operation
    (create / list / get / replace / patch / delete) is scoped to that
    project's users, regardless of which <code>Host</code> / auth-domain the
    request arrives on. The credential can never read or mutate another
    project's user pool. To provision more than one project, run one scoped
    credential per project.
  </p>

  <h2>external_id correlation</h2>
  <p>
    The user model carries a stable, IdP-owned
    <code>external_id</code> (SCIM <code>externalId</code>). It is unique per
    project when set and lets the IdP target an account independently of email
    changes. It round-trips through every store (Postgres, SQLite, in-memory)
    and is exposed on the <code>User</code> message
    (field&nbsp;25).
  </p>

  <h2>Supported surface</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>POST /scim/v2/Users</code> — create a user.</li>
    <li><code>GET /scim/v2/Users/&#123;id&#125;</code> — fetch one user.</li>
    <li>
      <code>GET /scim/v2/Users?filter=userName eq "a@b.com"</code> — list with
      <code>userName</code>, <code>email</code>, or <code>externalId</code> eq
      filters, plus <code>startIndex</code> / <code>count</code> pagination.
    </li>
    <li><code>PUT /scim/v2/Users/&#123;id&#125;</code> — replace a user.</li>
    <li>
      <code>PATCH /scim/v2/Users/&#123;id&#125;</code> — partial update of
      <code>userName</code>, <code>emails</code>/<code>email</code>,
      <code>name</code> (given/family/displayName), <code>externalId</code>, and
      <code>active</code> (the path Microsoft Entra ID drives all profile syncs
      through). <code>active:false</code> deactivates the account and
      immediately revokes its sessions and refresh tokens;
      <code>active:true</code> reactivates it. Unsupported attributes are
      rejected with <code>400</code>.
    </li>
    <li><code>DELETE /scim/v2/Users/&#123;id&#125;</code> — remove a user.</li>
    <li>
      <code>GET /scim/v2/ServiceProviderConfig</code>,
      <code>/Schemas</code>, <code>/ResourceTypes</code> — discovery.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Example: provision a user</h2>
  <Code
    lang="bash"
    code={`curl -X POST https://auth.example.com/scim/v2/Users \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $GATEWAY_SCIM_BEARER_TOKEN" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/scim+json" \\
  -d '{
    "schemas": ["urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:core:2.0:User"],
    "userName": "alice@example.com",
    "externalId": "okta-00u123",
    "name": { "givenName": "Alice", "familyName": "Smith" },
    "emails": [{ "value": "alice@example.com", "primary": true }],
    "active": true
  }'`}
  />

  <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/30 p-4 text-sm">
    <strong>Deferred.</strong> SCIM <code>/Groups</code> is not yet
    implemented. Each bearer token is scoped to one project
    (<code>GATEWAY_SCIM_PROJECT_ID</code>); multiplexing several projects
    through a single credential is intentionally out of scope. SCIM mutations
    write straight through the project-scoped repository, so they do not yet
    emit the service-layer audit events / user-lifecycle webhooks that the gRPC
    admin path does — a tracked follow-up. The <code>/Users</code> surface
    above is complete and tested across all storage backends.
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
